# Normalize line endings to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Why this matters: GitHub's Windows CI runners check out with
# core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF -> CRLF on checkout. Vitest's esbuild
# transform mishandles a `#!` shebang line that ends in CRLF and emits code
# V8 rejects with "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" — so a shebang'd
# module imported by a test (e.g. scripts/scan-history-secrets.mjs) fails to
# collect on windows-latest while macOS/Ubuntu (which keep LF) stay green.
# Forcing LF for text files keeps checkouts byte-identical across platforms
# and removes this class of failure for current and future files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Keep binaries untouched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
